Z||000002||Ronnie||04-14-2001||10:01 PM||||I just replaced my 86 GT power window glass on the passenger side. The glass doesn't matter if it's power or not , but be sure to get tinted if yours is already tinted. Standard coupes do not have tinted windows normally , but SE's and GT's do. I got mine from the Pull-a-Part yard, for about $5 bucks. Drill out the rivets with a 3/16ths drill, then punch out the rest of the rivet. Then I just drilled the hole out to 1/4 inch , and installed 1/4 inch screws with locking nuts. About a 2-3 hour job , but this was the first window replacement I'd ever done.<P>------------------<BR>'86GT/'88FORMULA/'88GT<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ronnies_1.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000003||FieroJoe||04-14-2001||10:59 PM||||I just had mine done professionally, they came out to the house to do it.  They put in the new glass with the rivets, but you'll only be able to find those big (and strong) rivets at a glass shop.  I believe they are all stainless steel.  He used a huge rivet gun about as big as a big bolt cutter, and then he was still pushing really hard.<P>So the 1/4 bolts will work well, be sure to use nylock nuts and locktite, just to be sure.<P>Replace dewstrips too if you need to!<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||jch82||04-15-2001||01:31 AM||||So its really that easy? Just drill out a few rivets and put in nuts and bolts? That seems almost to good to be true...<P>So your best bet to tint the windows is to actually take them out? Thanks<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Yeah, my girlfriend takes collect calls from the road<BR>And it doesn't seem to matter that I'm lacking in the bulge<BR>She laughs at my dumb jokes when no one does<BR>She brings me mexican food from Sombrero's just because<BR>                 <I>-Blink 182</I>||||reg||5
Z||000005||DXR_DAD||04-15-2001||10:47 AM||||Any more info????? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>THANKS<BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||5
Z||000006||Ronnie||04-15-2001||12:18 PM||||Not so easy to make it fun!!! LOL. But almost easy enough to take the window out to do the dew strips tho!!  Their a pain with the window in. <BR>You do need to raise and lower the window a little bit in order to get to all the rivets or screws, or else, they don't all line up with the openings at the same time. But no big deal.||||reg||6
